        {
          "id": 879836070,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "It was so, that you can hide interfaces like extcap, but don't have to reenable them if you just need them once. Also it's a UI thing. It states %n interfaces hidden, but you have to remember where to explicitly enable them to use them.\n\nAnd lastly, I hate when we have dead code, so either we reenable the feature (and fix the bug) or remove the feature and close the bug.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
